1|0@Volkswagen^1440785823#cuivz88:Bluetooth_Sandwich$:I think you're confusing reliability with "oh, that's broken, ok I'll fix it whenever" The biggest complainers about ANY German car are the too lazy to address issues early on when the car makes a noise or something seems off. In retrospect the Honda or Toyota is literally barebones when compared to their German counterpart. These cars can be just as reliable as the Japanese cars(there are exceptions no doubt), but when you ignore issues then they snowball into catastrophe issues. That's not the fault of the machine, it's the user. It's like blaming a computer for always getting viruses because you keep clicking the porn ads. One thing that seems to be apparent, at least to me, is the fact that Germany will try new design ideas with their motors or suspension. Whereas the Japanese have been building the same car for the last 40 years, not broke? don't fix it mentality. Which is fine, different strokes for different folks. 
